## Context
Finding (b) of the 0818 clone run (`verification/clone/0818-clone-rung-2026-09-23.json`):
8 035 existing `.zotero-sdt-cache` packs were rewritten on the first run.
Accounted for in `verification/clone/0818-findings-2026-09-24.md`:

- All 8 035 were written by processor `pdf@3` (8 028) or `epub@1` (7), the
  Zotero 10.0 constants; the run's Zotero 10.0.3 declares pdf 14 / epub 2
  (`SYNC.md`, extraction row). The stored source hash matches the file in all
  of them, so each is a `stale-processor` pack, and `ensure()`, which the
  sitter's census calls, regenerates it before resolving (ticket 0755's contract).
- Every one of the 5 672 current packs was kept byte-identical.
- The legacy `sdt-sitter-cache.jsonl` (5 672 rows, no `format` stamp, ticket
  0771) loaded 0 rows; that cost reads, not rewrites.

Not a sitter defect, and not a live-install blocker. It is the cost of the
first live run: the author's library was last opened by 10.0.3, so doudou
carries the same verdict, about 8 000 regenerations, 20 910 s (5,8 h) on padme.

## Exit criteria
- [x] `bench/pack_census.sh` (or the probe's pack tally) on doudou before the
      live install, the stale-processor count recorded in this log: native
      Zotero also regenerates a stale pack when a reader opens it, so the
      2026-09-22 copy's figure may have shrunk
- [x] The author told, before the install, how long the first run is expected to take
